1. (Currently Amended) A medical-device system, comprising:a risk stratification circuit configured to:
receive physiological information including respiration information and heart sound information sensed from a patient;
generate distinct first, second, and third signal metrics using the received physiological information, the first signal metric generated using the received respiration information, the second or the third signal metric generated using the received heart sound information;
calculate a primary pulmonary risk score using the first signal metric, and calculate a secondary pulmonary risk score using the second and the third signal metrics, the primary pulmonary risk score and the secondary pulmonary risk score each taking a numerical value;
and calculate a composite pulmonary risk score using the primary and the secondary pulmonary risk scores; and
an output a physiological event detector circuit configured to provide detect a cardiorespiratory event of the patient based at least in part on the calculated composite pulmonary risk to a user or a process score.
2. (Currently Amended) The medical-device system of claim 1, comprising a wherein the physiological event detector circuit is configured to determine or adjust a detection threshold based at least in part on the calculated composite pulmonary risk score, and to automatically detect [[a]]the cardiorespiratory event of the patient based at least in part on using the calculated composite pulmonary risk score determined or adjusted detection threshold.
3. (Currently Amended) The medical-device system of claim [[2]]1, wherein to automatically detect the cardiorespiratory event, the physiological event detector circuit is configured to:
calculate a cardiorespiratory event score using one or more physiological signals sensed from the patient;
determine or adjust an alert threshold based at least in part on the calculated composite pulmonary risk score; and
generate an alert of the cardiorespiratory event when the cardiorespiratory event score exceeds the alert threshold.
4. (Currently Amended) The medical-device system of claim [[2]]1, wherein the cardiorespiratory event includes at least one of worsening heart failure (WHF), chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), asthma, or pulmonary edema.
5. (Currently Amended) The medical-device system of claim 1, wherein the first, the second,- andor the third signal metrics are each metric is selected from the group consisting of:
a respiration rate;
a ratio of respiration rate to tidal volume;
a third heart sound (S3) intensity;
an intensity of a first (S1), a second (S2), or a third (S3) heart sound;
a timing of the Sl, the S2, or the S3 heart sound;
a Q wave to S2 interval;
an Si to S2 interval; or a ratio of the S3 intensity to a reference heart sound intensity;
a heart rate;
a thoracic impedance; and
a physical activity level.
6. (Currently Amended) The medical-device system of claim 1, wherein the risk stratification circuit is configured to calculate the secondary pulmonary risk score using measurements of the second signal metric obtained sampled only at times when the third signal metric satisfies a specified condition.
7. (Original) The medical-device system of claim 6, wherein the second signal metric include a respiratory rate and the third signal metric incudes a physical activity intensity or duration,
wherein the measurements of the second signal metric include respiratory rates measured during a time period when the physical activity intensity or duration exceeds a threshold.
8. (Original) The medical-device system of claim 1, wherein the risk stratification circuit is configured to calculate the secondary pulmonary risk score using the second signal metric weighted by the third signal metric.
9. (Original) The medical-device system of claim 1, wherein the risk stratification circuit is configured to calculate the composite pulmonary risk score using a linear or a nonlinear combination of the primary and secondary pulmonary risk scores.
10. (Original) The medical-device system of claim 1, wherein the risk stratification circuit is configured to calculate the composite pulmonary risk score using a neural network taking the primary and the secondary pulmonary risk scores as input.
11. (Canceled)
12. (Original) The medical-device system of claim 1, comprising a therapy circuit configured to initiate or adjust a therapy to treat a cardiorespiratory disease in accordance with the calculated composite pulmonary risk score.
