generating, via a risk stratification circuit of a medical-device system, distinct first, second, and third signal metrics using the received physiological information, the first signal metric generated using the received respiration information, the second or the third signal metric generated using the received heart sound information;
calculating, via the risk stratification circuit, a primary pulmonary risk score using the first signal metric, and calculate a secondary pulmonary risk score using the second and the third signal
metrics, the primary pulmonary risk score and the secondary pulmonary risk score each taking a numerical value;calculating, via the risk stratification circuit, a composite pulmonary risk score using the primary and the secondary pulmonary risk scores; and
providing, via an output circuit, automatically detecting, via a physiological event detector circuit, a cardiorespiratory event of the patient based at least in part on the calculated composite pulmonary risk to a user or a process score.
14. (Currently Amended) The method of claim 13, further comprising automatically detecting a cardiorespiratory event of the patient based at least in part on the calculated composite pulmonary risk score, wherein the cardiorespiratory event including includes at least one of worsening heart failure (WHF), chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), asthma, or pulmonary edema.
15. (Currently Amended) The method of claim [[14]]13, wherein automatically detecting the cardiorespiratory even includes:calculating a cardiorespiratory event score using one or more physiological signals sensed from the patient;
determining or adjusting an alert threshold based at least in part on the calculated composite pulmonary risk score; and
